      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Grate the potatoes coarsely. Working in batches, wrap in a clean tea towel and squeeze out as much liquid as you can over the sink. Transfer to a bowl."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the grated onion, eggs, flour, and seasoning to the potato. Mix well until combined."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat enough oil to cover the base of a large frying pan over medium-high heat. The oil should shimmer before you add the potato."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drop heaped spoonfuls of the mixture into the pan and press flat to about 1cm thick. Fry for 3 to 4 minutes until the underside is deep golden and crisp. Flip and cook for a further 3 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Drain on kitchen paper and keep warm in a low oven while you cook the remaining batches. Serve immediately with apple sauce and sour cream."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Pancakes are soggy rather than crisp"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Not enough moisture was squeezed out. Squeeze the grated potato until almost dry, or the pan was not hot enough when you added the mixture."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Pancakes fall apart in the pan"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Do not flip them too early. Wait until the edges look set and the underside is properly golden. The binding firms up as they cook."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Potato mixture turns grey"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "This is oxidation and does not affect taste. Grate and cook in quick succession, or squeeze dry and mix quickly once grated."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Kartoffelpuffer are sold at German Christmas markets from November to December, served in paper cones with apple sauce. They are also the Ashkenazi Jewish latke, eaten at Hanukkah with sour cream. The dish is beloved across Germany, Austria, and Eastern European Jewish communities. Simple and quick to make, they suit both a weekday meal and a festive occasion."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
